%% childsafe/self.glp --- the child-safe social network as a certified program
%% of its own (CSSN Section 8.1): the adult agent (agent.vglp) and the child
%% agent (child_agent.vglp), two vGLP modules that hand a party over to each
%% other, compiled beside their sources into agent.glp and child_agent.glp;
%% the cards they share (self.vglp, which joins this module as the program
%% loads); the mini-app entry cssn/3 (miniapp.glp); and the scripted person
%% (person.glp).  The types and the helpers are the parent's (../self.glp, an
%% ancestor scope).
%%
%% It is a program of its own because the certificate of a program is refused
%% where any entry point reaches the person or the network, and the parent's
%% plays do (send_to_user/1): loaded here, without them, the program is
%% certified, and its module value is the mini-app the super-app installs and
%% activates by run/3 (GSG paper, Section 3).

imported procedure miniapp#cssn(Key?, PersonChannel(Drawn)?, Stream(Conversation)?).
exported procedure cssn(Key?, PersonChannel(Drawn)?, Stream(Conversation)?).
cssn(Id, Ui, Convs) :- miniapp # cssn(Id?, Ui?, Convs?).
